#: llmcord_core/i18n/terms.py
msgid "**Blackjack in short**"
msgstr ""

#: llmcord_core/i18n/terms.py
msgid "Get closer to 21 than the dealer without going over."
msgstr ""

#: llmcord_core/i18n/terms.py
msgid "• Cards: 2–10 are face value, J/Q/K are 10, an ace is 1 or 11."
msgstr ""

#: llmcord_core/i18n/terms.py
msgid "• Hit takes a card. Stand keeps your hand."
msgstr ""

#: llmcord_core/i18n/terms.py
msgid "• Hit takes a card. Stand keeps your hand. Double doubles your bet, takes one card and ends your turn (first two cards only)."
msgstr ""

#: llmcord_core/i18n/terms.py
#, python-brace-format
msgid "• Over 21 is a bust: you lose. An ace with a ten-value card on your first two cards is blackjack and pays {ratio}."
msgstr ""

#: llmcord_core/i18n/terms.py
#, python-brace-format
msgid "• The dealer plays after everyone: it draws until {stand_on} or more."
msgstr ""

#: llmcord_core/i18n/terms.py
#, python-brace-format
msgid "• The dealer plays after everyone: it draws until {stand_on} or more, and also hits a soft 17."
msgstr ""

#: llmcord_core/i18n/terms.py
msgid "• Win: you get your bet back plus the same again. Tie: the dealer wins."
msgstr ""

#: llmcord_core/i18n/terms.py
msgid "• Win: you get your bet back plus the same again. Tie: your bet comes back."
msgstr ""

#: llmcord_core/i18n/terms.py
msgid "• Insurance: when the dealer shows an ace you may put up half your bet (bets of 2 or more) that the dealer has blackjack; it pays 2 to 1. With a blackjack you may take even money (paid 1 to 1 right away) instead."
msgstr ""

#: llmcord_core/i18n/terms.py
msgid "• Surrender: on your first two cards, once the dealer has checked for blackjack, you may give up the hand and get half your bet back."
msgstr ""

